# NOTE: docker build reads the .dockerignore at the BUILD CONTEXT ROOT, and this app's build
# context is the repo root (see the Dockerfile header), so this file is not consulted by the
# platform build - the Dockerfile COPYs an explicit file list instead. It is kept for local
# `docker build examples/_template` experiments and as the ignore an app inherits if it ever
# switches to an app-dir build context. Keeping the image lean is the goal either way.

# Installed deps (the image runs its own `npm ci` from the committed lockfile, #481).
node_modules/

# Tests never run inside the image.
*.test.js
tests/

# VCS + editor noise.
.git/
.gitignore
.DS_Store

# Docs and local-only files never needed inside the image.
README.md
*.md
.env
.env.*
